l_english:
##eaw
ship_hull_super_heavy_2: "Missile Super Heavy Battleship Hull"
semi_modern_ship_hull_super_heavy:"Missile Super Heavy Battleship"
##vnr
 annapolis_naval_academy: "Howlington Naval Academy"
 annapolis_naval_academy_desc: "Located in Howlington, Westshore, the Hippogriffia Naval Academy has a long history dated back to decades ago. The school encourages students to establish strategic visions around seapower through comprehensive education on naval tactics and technologies."
 dartmouth_naval_academy: "Equestria Naval War College"
 dartmouth_naval_academy_desc: "As old as the Equestrian Navy itself, the Equestria Naval Academy at Canterbury has been a symbol of Equestrian armed forces for centuries."
 murwik_naval_academy: "Marineschule Ditrysuim"
 murwik_naval_academy_desc: "Ditrysuim Naval Academy, or Marineschule Ditrysuim in Changelingia, is the main training establishment for all Changeling Navy officers after its replacement of Queen's Naval Academy in 996. The instituition aims at professionalizing Changeling naval officers through weapon systems training and naval engineering education."
 
 #equip_naval
 cruiser_equipment_3: "Interwar Cruiser"
 vnr_cruiser_cost_1: "Interwar Cruiser"
 vnr_ship_hull_light_1: "Storm-era Light Hull"
 early_ship_hull_cruiser: "Storm-era Cruiser Hull"
 vnr_ship_hull_cruiser_1: "Storm-era Cruiser Hull"
 early_ship_hull_heavy: "Storm-era Heavy Hull"
 vnr_ship_hull_heavy_1: "Storm-era Heavy Hull"
 vnr_ship_hull_submarine_1: "Storm-era Submarine Hull"
 vnr_ship_hull_submarine_1_desc: "The first submersible warships actually capable of effective combat actions, these designs are significant improvements over their predecessors. With diesel-electric engines replacing the primarily petrol-electric engines of the first submarines, they have greatly improved range and surface speed compared with their predecessors. In combat with enemy warships, they act mainly as submersible light torpedo boats, but lack the submerged speed or endurance to remain underwater for more than relatively brief periods. These are the submarines that were used by the major naval powers during the increasing global tension."
 vnr_ship_hull_submarine_2_desc: "The evolution of the earlier submarine designs, some of these warships took 'cruiser' submarines ideas further, with larger guns and a greater emphasis on surface abilities, while others look in the other direction, seeking to increase underwater capabilities and performance."
 vnr_ship_hull_submarine_3_desc: "The gains made by some earlier designs in extending underwater range, speed, and overall abilities, led to the turn in submarine development away from 'cruiser' types and back towards vessels with a greater emphasis on underwater capabilities. Vastly improved over earlier types, these submarines carry potent payloads of torpedoes and are a legitimate threat to almost all surface ships. However, they are still limited in submerged duration, range, and speed, and remain vulnerable when surfaced, especially to aircraft."
 vnr_ship_hull_submarine_4_desc: "With greatly increased battery capacity, advanced systems to refresh air while still submerged, and overall refined designs, these are the first submarines intended to be able to remain submerged for most of the duration of their time at sea. As such, they mark a massive shift in naval warfare, and the ascendancy of submarines to being true terrors. Such warships offer the ability to dominate the oceans to those nations that developed and deployed them."
 vnr_ship_hull_light_1_desc: "The increasing global tension brought a new demand for destroyers- not only were they required to protect their fleets, but they were also stretched thin to protect the Entente shipping lines as well. To meet this need, destroyer designs were streamlined, entering mass production to keep up with demand. Ships of this era are typically 1000 tons, and travel at a top speed of 34 knots, while carrying a larger pair of torpedoes than their forebears."
 vnr_ship_hull_light_2_desc: "The trend during increasing global tension had been towards larger destroyers with heavier armaments. A number of opportunities to fire at capital ships had been missed during the war, because destroyers had expended all their torpedoes in an initial salvo. To address this, destroyers were strengthened in terms of hull and armament. Destroyers in this period had larger hulls with a displacement of about 1,500 to 2,000 tons, led by slightly larger destroyer leader."
 vnr_ship_hull_light_3_desc: "By 1010, with increasingly potent new aircraft designs entering service, as well as several navies deploying more carriers, while there was still some doubt about just how useful the carriers would be in open warfare, concern over the potential threat that aircraft might pose to warships was growing. Continued exercises had shown the world that the carrier has a purpose in the navy. As a result, destroyers saw the introduction of the dual purpose primary armament, granting a vastly improved anti-aircraft role to the destroyer, again increasing their usefulness. These ships, displacing up to 2,500 tons, often carry increased payloads of torpedoes to offset the reduced torpedo load-out on more modern cruisers."
 vnr_ship_hull_light_4_desc: "With the increasing global tension, the world's navies needed cheap anti-aircraft platforms. The success with carrier combat had shown the world that they are suited for more than just recon and anti-carrier duties and they are required for modern anti-capital ship warfare. Advanced anti-submarine technologies also are playing an essential role in combating the major threat to convoy operations, they and the anti-aircraft platforms intensified demands for more destroyers. While previously destroyer investments were being lowered in favour of cruisers and the new battlecruisers, destroyers begin to return to the fore as an essential part of both the fleet, and the convoy system. Often not larger than their predecessors they are far more technologically advanced, mostly adopting flush decks and far larger torpedo armaments."
 vnr_ship_hull_light_5_desc: "Near the end of the global tension, the navies of the world were forced to adapt to new submarines that can stay submerged for almost indefinite periods of time, carriers which are loaded full of planes more than capable of destroying capital ships, with big gun cruisers quickly becoming irrelevant in the face of carriers and submarines. The future role of the escort for the fleet is being taken over almost solely by destroyers in the minds of most naval theorists, with dual purpose rapid firing turrets destroying any planes that dare cross her path in an attempt to dive bomb her. The displacement of these vessels was increased as well, often coming up to 3,000 tons as designers load them with more and more anti-aircraft weapons, as well as more primary guns."
 torpedo_cruiser_desc: "Based on the Jeune École ('Young School') doctrine which held that small warships armed with torpedoes can effectively and cheaply defeat much larger battleships, these cruisers are primarily armed with torpedoes. Most of the torpedo cruisers fell out of favour in most of navies in the 1890s, though many other navies continued to acquire them into the early 1900s. The modern torpedo cruisers are designed to use torpedoes that submarines cannot carry."
 early_ship_hull_cruiser_desc: "Until the end of the 9th century, unprotected cruisers still occupied a place in the fleet, while protected cruisers with armor began to emerge, and larger armored cruisers gradually entered the navy's sight. The rapid development of cruisers in the early 20th century had several types with various sizes, from the battlecruiser with firepower and protection close to a dreadnought, to the flotilla leaders which acted alongside destroyers, these cutting-edge cruisers have greatly surpassed the capital ships of the past."
 vnr_ship_hull_cruiser_1_desc: "Until the end of the 9th century, unprotected cruisers still occupied a place in the fleet, while protected cruisers with armor began to emerge, and larger armored cruisers gradually entered the navy's sight. The rapid development of cruisers in the early 20th century had several types with various sizes, from the battlecruiser with firepower and protection close to a dreadnought, to the flotilla leaders which acted alongside destroyers, these cutting-edge cruisers have greatly surpassed the capital ships of the past."
 vnr_ship_hull_cruiser_2_desc: "Naval construction in the early 1000s was limited by pacifism in most countries. With limited budget, the construction of ships with a high displacement and calibre guns is limited."
 vnr_ship_hull_cruiser_3_desc: "The interwar period saw refinements of cruisers within the frame of Washington Naval Treaty. With politics and finances still constraining many naval powers, the produced designs are only slightly larger in size than the previous generation, instead seeing upgrades in firepower through the use of bigger guns or the growing adoption of triple turrets and quadruple torpedo tubes. The growing importance of aviation in naval warfare also led to the adoption of high-angle dual-purpose mounts, supplemented by a growing array of autocannons. However, there were already some attempts to break the limits set on cruisers.\n\nInstall §YLarge Cruiser Role§! on §YCruiser Hull§! to unlock §YLarge Cruiser Battery§! and §YLarge Cruiser Armor§!."
 vnr_ship_hull_cruiser_4_desc: "Thanks to increased available funding, the new cruisers built at the end of the interwar period and the beginning of the Second increasing global tension again increased in size. While the primary armament's calibre remained unchanged once more, with few exceptions, their firepower was increased further by adding an extra turret or raising the number of guns in each turret. Secondary armaments was upgraded with further twin dual-purpose guns and even more dedicated anti-aircraft armament, often linked with improved fire controls. This generation also see the growing adoption of radar systems on cruisers."
 vnr_ship_hull_cruiser_5_desc: "The cruisers of the late-war and early post-war period remain similar to the ones of the early war, while incorporating the numerous lessons learned throughout. With aircraft confirmed to be one of the greatest threats to ships, designers focused on improving AA capabilities even further through better fire-control, improving coordination between batteries and radar. Some navies are also experimenting with autoloading mechanisms for the main armament, dramatically improving their rates of fire."
 early_ship_hull_heavy_desc: "Designed shortly before the increasing global tension began, and completed while it raged, these classes represent the highest level of naval development prior to the start of that conflict. They were the fleet-leading warships of the war, and remain highly potent long after it ended. While they are notably faster than the Dreadnoughts before them, their most notable differentiating feature is their escalated armament- they carry eight to ten main guns, most in twin turrets but a few in new triple turrets. Their devastating firepower and heavy armour guaranteed that they would be at the heart of their battle fleets in increasing global tension, but those continued advances came at quickly escalating prices. Even more so than the warships before them these classes demanded huge investments, though they were only shadow of what was to come."
 vnr_ship_hull_heavy_1_desc: "Designed shortly before the increasing global tension began, and completed while it raged, these classes represent the highest level of naval development prior to the start of that conflict. They were the fleet-leading warships of the war, and remain highly potent long after it ended. While they are notably faster than the Dreadnoughts before them, their most notable differentiating feature is their escalated armament- they carry eight to ten main guns, most in twin turrets but a few in new triple turrets. Their devastating firepower and heavy armour guaranteed that they would be at the heart of their battle fleets in increasing global tension, but those continued advances came at quickly escalating prices. Even more so than the warships before them these classes demanded huge investments, though they were only shadow of what was to come."
 vnr_ship_hull_heavy_2_desc: "The inter-war period saw the battleship subjected to strict limitation due to prevent another war breaking out. However, Faced with the prospect of a naval arms race against the Changeling and Griffonia, which would in turn have led to a possible naval war in both East and West, the Equestria was keen to conclude the pacifism in early 1000s. This pacifism makes multiple countries focused on various civilian ship and lightindustries thus restricted the number and size of battleships that each major nation built. Designs like the Equestria Star Swirl class battleship and the Hippogriffia Queen Novo class—all of which continued the trend to larger ships with bigger guns and thicker armor—never got off the drawing board. Those designs which were commissioned during this period were referred to as inter-war battleships."
 vnr_ship_hull_heavy_3_desc: "The naval powers extensively upgraded and modernized their Storm–era battleships during the early 1000s. Among the new features were an increased tower height and stability for the optical rangefinder equipment (for gunnery control), more armor (especially around turrets) to protect against plunging fire and aerial bombing, and additional anti-aircraft weapons. Even when war threatened again in the late 1930s, battleship construction did not regain the level of importance it had held in the years before increasing global tension. The "building holiday" imposed by the naval treaties meant the capacity of dockyards worldwide had shrunk, and the strategic position had changed."
 vnr_ship_hull_heavy_4_desc: "With the increasing global tension on the horizon and international tensions higher than ever, designers are looking to construct a new generation of ships to fight in the upcoming war. While some nations had transitioned their naval hopes to carriers, others still insist that the carrier can only provide a supplementary role, rather than replacing the primary anti-capital ship role of the battleship. These nations instead retool their newer designs, focusing on improved armour layouts and more effective guns and turrets, as well as improved speeds."
 vnr_ship_hull_heavy_5_desc: "At the close of the increasing global tension, the Great Powers started to understand: naval air power had proved victorious over all gun capital ships. However, several nations persist with the development of Battleships, as shore bombardment platforms, prestige projects and support for carriers within the fleet or even try to promote their old role. Some designers load their battleships with anti-aircraft batteries to increase the chances of survival. Although many of these battleships may continue to operate for many years, they are already viewed as obsolete by some nations."
 vnr_ship_hull_carrier_1_desc: "Developed in the early1000s, these ships are designed to provide aerial reconnaissance and light fighter coverage for fleets primarily focused on more 'conventional' warship forces. Their range is significantly increased, and efforts were made to make them fast enough to keep up with fleets operating at full speed in open oceans."
 vnr_ship_hull_carrier_2_desc: "As major naval combat operations in the naval aviation age demonstrated the power of aircraft to seriously affect battles at sea, many powers found themselves having fallen behind in the development of their carrier forces. While fleet carriers are quickly shown to be the most potent of their kin, they are also massive ships that require a long time and large amount of resources to construct. In the rush to increase their ability to project air power into the oceans, the naval powers turned to designs like these, enlarged versions of the existing lighter carriers, to try to quickly bolster their naval aviation capacity."
 vnr_ship_hull_carrier_3_desc: "Continued development of carrier design led to much larger models, these ships are approaching the size of the first fleet carriers, while incorporating all of the design improvements made in the intervening years. Most have significant armour protection and withering AA firepower, while also being highly mechanically reliable. However, they abandoned concept of large calibre secondary armament in exchange for smaller dual purpose guns."
 vnr_ship_hull_super_heavy_1_desc: "The rapid increase of resources devoted to naval construction after the end of major land conflict during the Storm King's invasion initially produced these designs, which featured the beginnings of the trends towards sudden growth in size, firepower, armour, calibre and of course, cost. Such vessels set the world's leading naval powers apart from the mere pretenders to greatness, but they have their issues; their rapid development and rushed construction led to design flaws and persistent mechanical problems. These designs are armed with eight to ten 18 inch or equivalent main guns, and have the protection to go toe-to-toe with similarly armed ships. As the Naval Holiday came, these monsters were buried by time."
 ship_hull_cruiser_desc: "Near the end of the 9th century, cruiser came to be a classification of the ships intended for cruising distant waters, for commerce raiding, and for scouting for the battle fleet. It came in a wide variety of sizes, from smaller protected cruiser to large armored cruiser. With the advent of the dreadnought battleship before World War, armored cruiser had gradually evolved into battlecruiser, while the direct successors to protected cruisers can be placed on a consistent scale of warship size until the London Naval Conference officially set the standards for light and heavy cruisers."

 ship_hull_heavy_desc: "Before the Storm King's Invasion, the navy had already seen battleships with 15-inch guns, which was one of the largest war machines ever built in human history. Designed for maximum firepower and survivability, these leviathans dominate every inch of the waters."

 ship_hull_carrier_0: "Storm-era Carrier Hull"
 vnr_ship_hull_carrier_conversion_bb_desc: "The first large aircraft carriers, these ships are mainly built on hulls that were originally intended for capital warships but, because of the Storm King's Invasion, converted and completed as carriers. Only a handful of navies built such ships, and their designs varied greatly; their aircraft capacities ranged from the low sixties to a hundred. There are constants though, such as retained heavily armoured belts and other gun-warship features. Semi-experimental and unreliable, they are still incredibly formidable weapons, and laid the foundations for following generations of fleet carriers."
 ship_hull_submarine_desc: "A far cry from the crude boats of the Storm-era, the modern submarine is more capable than ever before and can threaten even the biggest ship for a very moderate cost."
 vnr_ship_hull_pre_dreadnought_desc: "Followed the design of the Equestria Majestic-class of the late 980s, Pre-Dreadnought battleships replaced the ironclad battleships of the 970s. Built from steel, and protected by hardened steel armour, pre-dreadnought battleships carry a main battery of very heavy guns in barbettes supported by one or more secondary batteries of lighter weapons.\n\nSince the 'Dreadnought' design made them obsoleted since before the Great War, coupled with the gigantic rise of Dreadnought-based designs in the previous three decades, only a few of them are still in service."
 vnr_ship_hull_cruiser_panzerschiff_desc: "As a radical measure to hide rearmament from Equestria, the Admiralitat first adopted panzerschiff (armored ship) as temporary capital ships. Having an intermediate firepower between heavy cruisers and battlecruisers, the panzerschiff heralded quite an advantage in an one-on-one combat against cruisers, but it would be rendered useless facing an organized fleet."
 vnr_ship_hull_light_6_desc: "After the Great War, conventional destroyers built during this period were significantly larger than wartime ships and had fully automatic main guns, unit machinery, radar, sonar, and antisubmarine weapons such as the squid mortar. The advent of surface-to-air missiles and surface-to-surface missiles in the 1020s changed naval warfare. Guided missile destroyers were developed to carry these weapons and protect the fleet from air, submarine, and surface threats."
 vnr_ship_hull_cruiser_6_desc: "The rise of air power during Great War dramatically changed the nature of naval combat. Even the fastest cruisers can not maneuver quickly enough to evade aerial attack, and aircraft now had torpedoes, allowing moderate-range standoff capabilities.\n\nWith battleships completely outdated in the advent of missiles, cruisers became the largest capital ships in the world after 1020s. Some of them adopted full missile designs and even applied nuclear engines."
 vnr_ship_hull_submarine_5_desc: "In the 1020s, nuclear power partially replaced diesel–electric propulsion. Equipment was also developed to extract oxygen from sea water. These two innovations gave submarines the ability to remain submerged for weeks or months."
 vnr_ship_hull_mega_carrier_desc: "By the late 1910s, nuclear weapons had been put into use in real combat. Its horrible power unleashed upon populated cities had forced every major country to develop and deploy tools of nuclear triad. Heavy jet bombers were the only way to send nuclear bombs to distant location before the advent of inter-continential missiles. It prompted navy to propose a mobile platform of launching nuclear raids, which was the strike carrier."
 vnr_ship_hull_arsenal_ship_desc: "Development and mass production of rockets has made missiles even cheaper than other measures of war. The concept of a large surface ships carrying hundreds of missiles was brought up to engage in heavy and accurate shore bombardment. Some experts called it the arsenal ship."
 
 
 #research
 large_destroyer_trend_desc: "A flotilla leader is a warship suitable for commanding a flotilla of destroyers or other small warships, typically a small cruiser or a large destroyer. Originally, the role was usually played by light cruisers or scout cruisers, but the rapid growth of destroyers in the late 990s has made these vessels obsolete and incapable of keeping pace with faster destroyers. The new dynamics at sea had prompted navies to build dedicated large destroyers to replace them.\n\nInstall §YDestroyer Leader Role§! on §YLight Hull§! to strengthen §YLight Attack§!."
 escort_destroyer_trend_desc: "During the Storm King Invasion, the emergence of new submarines posed a major threat to the merchant fleets. As a large number of destroyers were occupied on the frontline, the demand for an economical and flexible light destroyer became urgent. Escort destroyers have been stripped of most unnecessary equipments, retaining only basic guns and depth charges, any naval power can build numerous ships of this type within a few months. With sonars, these little guys active on the ocean route have become an important factor in the country's war potential.\n\nInstall §YEscort Destroyer Role§! on §YLight Hull§! to reduce §YCost§!."
 destroyer_missile_upgrade_desc: "During Late Aris War, efforts were started to develop surface-to-air missiles as it was generally considered that flak was of little use against bombers of ever-increasing performance. The research was led by several major powers in the world and quickly developed a great amount of types.Modified upon land-based SAM system, the ship-to-air missile system saw dedicated improvements in its guiding and launching modules.\n\nInstall §YAnti-Air Destroyer Role§! on §YLight Hull§! to unlock §YSurface-to-Air Missiles§!."
 early_cruiser_armor: "Storm-era Cruiser Armor"
 early_cruiser_armor_desc: "In the late 990s, it had become a trend that cruisers with armor protection will replace unprotected cruisers, which pointed out the future of cruisers.\n\nMounting this module on §YCruisers§! improves their ability to §Ywithstand enemy damage§!, but also §Rreduces§! their §Yspeed§!."
 basic_cruiser_armor_desc: "The restriction on displacement of cruisers made by Washington Naval Treaty in the 1920s promoted the naval designers to adopt ideas, such as inclined armor, to save the tonnage. Newly designed cruisers generally had moderate armor, which can resist shells from old rapid-fire guns.\n\nMounting this module on §YCruisers§! improves their ability to §Ywithstand enemy damage§!, but also §Rreduces§! their §Yspeed§!."
 treaty_cruiser_trend: "Inter-war Cruiser"
 treaty_cruiser_trend_desc: "With the concern that a subsequent war provoked by building larger, more powerful cruisers might subvert the usefulness of the prohibition on capital ship construction, many countries set limits on the tonnage and firepower of cruiserin displacement and maximum main gun caliber, further solidating the modern definition of cruiser."
 cruiser_gun_upgrade_desc: "Facing stronger performance of destroyers in the early 1000s, rapid-fire guns developed before the war can no longer meet the needs. To ensure efficiency against destroyers, cruisers are equipped with mechanical loading machines that increase rate of fire while saving manpower. Although the machine still requires manual assistance, it can achieve a loading efficiency far exceeding that of non-autoloading guns."
 cruiser_aa_upgrade_desc: "By the 1005, carrier-based aircrafts have seen great progress in capacity and payload. From the many naval-aeronautic exercises held, some naval officers have seen the dominance of aircraft carriers in future naval warfare. To counter it, most ships are reinforced with better anti-air firepower, and constructions of dedicated anti-air cruisers start simultaneously.\n\nInstall §YAnti-Air Cruiser Role§! on §YCruiser Hull§! to strengthen §YAnti-Air Attack§!."
 helipad_desc: "The idea of helicopter was invented way before the 10th century, but hundreds of them were first built and deployed in the war during the Second World War. At first, helicopters were used in small numbers for observation, transport, and medical evacuation. As vertical flight would save more space on a narrow deck of ship, the navy also saw this breakthrough as a perfect replenishment for seaplanes. But before turboshaft was developed, helicopters only played a very limited role in naval opearations."
 basic_heavy_armor_desc: "After the end of Storm King Invasion, capital ships began to adopt thicker armor to cope with the rapid advancement of naval guns. The armor belts of front-line battleships can usually reach a thickness of more than 300 mm, which was able to basically defend against the shooting of main guns built during the war.\n\nMounting this module on §YHeavy Ships§! improves their ability to §Ywithstand enemy damage§!. §YBattleships§! and §YBattlecruisers§! are defined by their different §YArmors§!."
 improved_heavy_armor_desc: "In the 1000s, inclined armor was applied on the newly designed capital ships. Despite a slightly inferior thickness, it can achieve a similar level of protection as thicker vertical armor.\n\nMounting this module on §YHeavy Ships§! improves their ability to §Ywithstand enemy damage§!. §YBattleships§! and §YBattlecruisers§! are defined by their different §YArmors§!."

 incremental_armor_scheme: "Post-Seaquestria Armor Scheme"
 incremental_armor_scheme_desc: "The Battle of Seaquestria has proved armor layout before 1001 incompetent. Lacking awareness of the long combat distance, the armor of previous battleships generally lacked the ability to resist 15-inch naval guns. The new armor scheme developed after that was also known as the post-Seaquestria scheme. It was just a temporary design strengthening the deck armor, and soon became obsolete after the war.\n\nInstall §YArmor Scheme§! on §YHeavy Hull§! to strengthen §YArmor§! or §YHP§!."
 mixed_armor_scheme_desc: "The mixed scheme is a transitional armor scheme after the war, which mainly integrated lessons learned from Seaquestria and the idea of all-or-nothing defense. Compared with the incremental scheme invented 20 years ago, it has a better armor ratio in some areas that are highly vulnerable.\n\nInstall §YArmor Scheme§! on §YHeavy Hull§! to strengthen §YArmor§! or §YHP§!."
 all_or_nothing_armor_scheme_desc: "The all-or-nothing scheme was first adopted on the Queen Novo-class battleships, and has been applied on all hippogriffia battleships after that. The all-or-nothing design greatly saves the armor of non-essential areas with the same tonnage, and uses armored citadel to protect the fragile magazine and main engine. Ships with this type of armor scheme usually have better survivability.\n\nInstall §YArmor Scheme§! on §YHeavy Hull§! to strengthen §YArmor§! or §YHP§!."
 all_or_nothing_armor_box_armor_scheme_desc: "During the first Changeling invasion of Equestria, higher level that all-or-nothing scheme was widely used, prompting a series of shells with stronger armor piercing effect. The secondary armor box works as a part to enhance the overall strength of the ship while protecting secondary areas such as crew quarters.\n\nInstall §YArmor Scheme§! on §YHeavy Hull§! to strengthen §YArmor§! or §YHP§!."
 harvey_steel: "Calm Steel"
 harvey_steel_desc: "Calm armor was a type of steel armor developed by Equestrian engineer Calm Water in the early 990s. It was once popular and saw several main producers of the armor plate including Shoals, Eiskaltenseen and Clawes."
 krupp_steel: "Eiskaltenseen Armor"
 krupp_steel_desc: "Eiskaltenseen armor was invented by Changeling's Eiskaltenseen Arm Works in 994 and replaced Calm armor as a primary method of protecting naval ships. The manufacturing of Eiskaltenseen armor was very similar to Harveyized armor, but the Eiskaltenseen process, instead of generally using nickel-steel, added as much as 1% chromium to the alloy for additional hardness. Early ballistic tests showed that 260mm of Eiskaltenseen armor offered the same protection as 300mm of Calm armor."
 krupp_cemented_steel: "Eiskaltenseen Cemented Armor"
 krupp_cemented_steel_desc: "The manufacturing process of Eiskaltenseen cemented armor (ECA) remained largely the same as original Eiskaltenseen steel armor, with slight changes in the alloy composition. The ECA retained the hardened surface via the application of carbonized gases but also had a much greater fibrous elasticity on the rear of the plate, which greatly reduced the incidence of spalling and cracking under incoming fire."
 ducol_steel: "Ducol Steel"
 ducol_steel_desc: "Ducol or D-steel is the name of a number of high-strength low-alloy steels of varying composition, first developed from the early 1920s by the Southern Equestria firm of Vernon & Sons. Applications have included ship hull construction, light armoring and pressure vessels such as locomotive steam boilers."
 homogeneous_krupp_steel: "Homogeneous Eiskaltenseen Armor"
 homogeneous_krupp_steel_desc: "Developments in face-hardened armor in the late 9th and early 10th centuries revealed that such armor was less effective against glancing oblique impacts. The hardened face layer's brittleness was counterproductive against such impacts. The new invention of homogeneous steel combined ductility and tensile strength, and was typically used for deck and waterline protection."
 dry_dock_expansion_desc: "As the scale of battleship projects escalating immediately after the Storm King's Invasion, dockyards for dreadnoughts can no longer fulfill the mission. To accommodate the huge hulls, shipbuilding enterprises decide to expand their dry docks built in the early 10th century.\nAlthough these super battleships are never launched, the docks remain active with capability of providing maintainence to a large ship or multiple small ships at the same time."
 enhanced_horizontal_defense_desc: "The parabolic trajectory from long distance is one of the most common ways to hit a ship in naval battles. The Battle of Seaquestria has already rendered deck armor of battleships weak, and thereby pushed the naval powers to enhance their horizontal protection. After studying outcomes of the battle at Seaquestria, naval powers all chose to strengthen battleship's deck armor."
 ship_living_standard_desc: "The living environment aboard was very harsh, but this situation is gradually changing. More countries begin to use iron beds and air-conditioning systems on warships to ensure the fighting will and physical condition of sailors in peacetime, so that they can devote themselves to the battle in a fuller state.\nMoreover, from carrot cakes and apple juice in Equestria to macaroni and ice cream in Hippogriffionia, food on ships is getting even better, though the best are reserved for officers. \n\n§CLet the army envy us!§!"
 prototype_airplane_launcher_desc: "The ship airplane launcher, invented by Equestria, uses hydraulic pressure to eject light seaplanes from ships with limited space, and then recovers them with a crane at the tail. Some countries have experimented with the application of seaplanes during the Great War and proved their power, but with the increasing size of aircrafts, conventional catapult can no longer sustain effective combat payload of the plane, which eventually inspires aircraft carrier in the future."
 folding_wing_desc: "The naval battle of the Great War was a three-dimensional form of combat, and the role played by plane was crucial. To achieve greater capacity on carriers, aviation designers applied folding wings on airplanes to save deck and hangar space, but this required high craftsmanship on the wings."
 air_fuel_storage_desc: "More extensive carrier opearations during the Great War urged carriers to have larger fuel tanks, while the quantity of air fuel aboard is also crucial to the range and loads of carrier-based aircrafts.\nMore air fuel carried usually means the carrier can support more air groups efficiently.\n\nAir fuel storage can help §Ycarrier-based aircrafts§! improve §Yrange§! and §Yagility§!."
 full_armored_carrier_desc: "The Equestria was the first to adopt armored flight decks on carriers before the war, which the armor can prevent dive bombing from damaging the deck in combat. This idea was quickly adopted by other naval powers in the war, and their new carriers were all reinforced with armored decks. Carriers nowadays have started to be characterized by fully enclosed hangars and heavily armored decks."
 carrier_angled_deck_desc: "The angled deck appeared in the late 1000s and was usually located on the left side of the flight deck, forming an angle of 6 to 13 degrees with the centerline. The entire flight deck was divided into two areas, allowing the carrier to perform take-off and landing operations at the same time, which greatly improves the sortie efficiency."
 basic_periscope_desc: "Periscopes have been used as early as 994 on Germany's first submarine, which can observe the situation on the water without surfacing."
 experimental_super_heavy_battery_desc: "In 985, Admiral Cabbage Fish proposed a super large battlecruiser to the Royal Navy, known as the HMS Incomparable. The design was intended to mount 20-inch guns, which would have been the largest ever mounted on a warship. However, the later research on 18-inch guns met various problems and ended. Countries including Equestria and Changeling re-initiated developement of 20-inch guns during the war, but have never come up with a functional model."
 large_shipyard_desc: "Increasing investments in the shipbuilding industry in the 9th century have brought dramatic changes to those enterprises when seapower became one of the most decisive factors in a country's strength. Small companies gradually got eliminated or annexed by industrial tycoons. The leading enterprises owned the largest shipyards in the world with ability to complete orders of several advanced warships at the same time."
 joint_sea_hospital_desc: "With skyrocketing casualties on the frontline during the Great War, the field hospitals are less than sufficient to treat the wounded. The hospital ships are deployed at sea, far from the battlefield, and can relieve the overloaded hospitals on land."
 rocket_depth_charges_desc: "To counter the new post-Great War submarines which run quieter, at much higher speed and can attack from much longer range with high speed homing torpedoes, modern anti-submarine weapon system is in desperate need to expand its range and sensors. The Rocket Assisted Torpedo (RAT) can be delievered by rocket engine, which allows warships the stand-off capability to attack hostile submarines with very little advance notice to them.\n\nMounting this module on §YLight Ships§! and §YCruisers§! will allow them to attack enemy §YSubmarines§!."
 destroyer_hull_improvement_desc: "Destroyer, emerged as an escort of capital ships in the late 990s century, has grown into the de facto capital ship of a modernized fleet in the second half of the century, carrying out all kinds of missions that were designated to cruisers or even battleships. It has proved to be an economical multi-role ship which will play an important role in the future."
 new_ship_materials_desc: "Since the Great War, naval armour has been less important due to the development of guided missiles. Missiles can be highly accurate and penetrate even the thickest of armor. Instead of investing more money in protection, new materials will be lighter, allowing the ship to sail at higher speed."
 nuclear_reactor_cost_reduction_desc: "The fission reactor marked the jewel of Ponies's industrial power when the world is heading towards the 1020s. In an attempt to build a full-nuclear fleet, new materials and devices are developed to reduce the cost of ship nuclear reactor."
 naval_tactical_data_system_desc: "Naval Tactical Data System (NTDS) is a computerized information processing system developed in the 1020s for use in combat ships. It takes reports from multiple sensors on different ships and collates it to produce a single unified map of the battlespace. This information can then be relayed back to the ships and to the weapons operators."
 recon_drones_desc: "An unmanned aerial vehicle (UAV), commonly known as a drone, is an aircraft without any pony pilot, crew, or passengers on board. UAVs were originally developed through the 2nd half of 10th century for military missions too \"dull, dirty or dangerous\" for humans. Naval powers developed their own unmanned fixed wing aerial vehicle or helicopter to undertake the duty of recon and anti-submarine warfare."
 unmanned_gun_turret_desc: "By the 1020s, gun turrets were increasingly unmanned, with gun laying controlled remotely from the ship's control centre using inputs from radar and other sources."
 modern_generic_battery_desc: "Naval Automatic Gun System was an automatic dual-purpose weapon system developed by New Marelandian military immediately after the Great War. The revolution of jet technology saw great improvement in the speed of aircrafts in the late-war period when a jet plane can fly at speeds close to 1,000 kilometres per hour, rendering anti-air guns ineffective against it. With fire-control computers and quick-firing guns, NAG can fire enough rounds in a short period to ensure a hit."
 coldwar_ship_torpedo_launcher_desc: "Because of improved submarine strength and speed, post-Great War torpedoes were given improved warheads and better motors.\n\nMounting this module on §YLight Ships§! or §YCruisers§! allows them to do significant damage to enemy §YCapital Ships§!."s
 close_in_area_air_defense_desc: "During the Great War, naval fleet was often faced with low-altitude air threats posed by suicide planes and radio-guided cruise missiles. With rehabilitation and modernization of wartime destroyers, they will be the last barrier against these threats."
 medical_supply_at_sea_desc: "During the Feathistian colonization golden age, the ill-prepared Nieuw Rottendestaat invasion has warned every nation of the weak points in trans-oceanic supplyline. When the medications reach the other side of the ocean, they sometimes corrupt due to extreme environments. By installing improved medical storage on boats, it will be helpful in long-range cruises and amphibious operations."
 sub_nuclear_engine_desc: "The conceptual design of the first nuclear submarine began in the late 1010s as the advance in nuclear technology allowed smaller power plant to be installed on platforms such as submarines. Designed as a pressurized water reactor, the new submarine reactor can offer infinite range, making the submerging time to be theoretically forever long."
 ##Crystal guns
 ship_heavy_crystal_projectile_module: "Twin Crystalline 406mm Cannon"
 ship_medium_crystal_projectile_module: "Triple Crystalline 190mm Cannon"
 ship_light_crystal_projectile_module: "Single Crystalline 127mm Cannon(Auto)"